Sval: Favorites' autofill is grouped as the address bar's own autofill

Sval's Favorites live in the engine's document, not in Places, so
`UrlbarProviderAutofill` finds none of them. `SvalFavoritesAutofill` fills
a favorite's origin or address in its place, as Firefox fills a bookmarked
one, and its result has to rank where Firefox's does. No API assigns a
heuristic result's group: `UrlbarUtils.getResultGroup` names each heuristic
provider it knows, and sends any other to the fallback group with a console
error. One case label puts it beside Firefox's own autofill.

diff --git a/browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarUtils.sys.mjs b/browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarUtils.sys.mjs
index e4ef360762..663f068056 100644
--- a/browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarUtils.sys.mjs
+++ b/browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarUtils.sys.mjs
@@ -607,6 +607,7 @@ export var UrlbarUtils = {
         case "UrlbarProviderAliasEngines":
           return this.RESULT_GROUP.HEURISTIC_ENGINE_ALIAS;
         case "UrlbarProviderAutofill":
+        case "SvalFavoritesAutofill":
           return this.RESULT_GROUP.HEURISTIC_AUTOFILL;
         case "UrlbarProviderBookmarkKeywords":
           return this.RESULT_GROUP.HEURISTIC_BOOKMARK_KEYWORD;
